{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous","id":1539068,"title":"Which of the Clans is the most dangerous","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-22T17:26:29-07:00","id":1539068,"title":"Which of the Clans is the most dangerous","content":"As it says in the title which of the clans do you think is the most dangerous in a variety of contexts including against kine, other kindred, other splats, politically? Basically, any way you can think of violence or domination of some kind, and why? I know it is open but that's the point for the purposes of conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","name":"Carsusbloodking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T18:31:19-07:00","id":1539072,"title":"","content":"For clans that can strike you from numerous fronts as well as your mortal family I would go with the Ventrue, Toreador and Lasombra clans being the most dangerous in that regard due to amount of influence they can gain in mortal society.<br /> <br /> Ones that can learn very dirty secrets that you don't want known then it's the Nosferatu and Followers Of Set who could get you do things that you don't want to, but wise members of these clans don't use that tactic all that often and find other means to get you to do what they wish done.<br /> <br /> Clans that can give and take a pounding would be the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> The Malkavians, Ravnos and Tzismce are the most dangerous to messing up your sense of reality with there horrorfic disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T20:45:06-07:00","id":1539079,"title":"","content":"My top 3 scariest clans:<br /> Ventrue are scary. Dominate, Presence and Fortitude. They can control your mind and your emotions and you can't even hurt them back.<br /> <br /> Tzimisci are scary in the &quot;I have no mouth and I must scream&quot; sort of way, based on the sorts of fucked up things that they can do to you via Vissicitude. They're also scary because you never really know what to expect when you face off against one.<br /> <br /> Ravnos are terrifying because you never know what's real or what isn't. You tell the Ravnos to disarm himself and he tosses a gun at your feet. Is that a gun or is it a grenade? You've got 3 seconds to decide... two seconds... one second...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T00:58:04-07:00","id":1539086,"title":"","content":"If I had to rate the clans on the subject of scale when it comes to danger, I would say that following are my top picks (V20).<br /> <br /> 1. Giovanni<br /> Clan founder is awake and actively directing the clan, they have Dominate and Potence which covers power, and they are one of the richest clans. They are not bound by faction issues and they use Necromancy which clans who lack that power can't fight. But then there is the big plan to bring down the barrier between the living world and the lands of the dead, which would see most of the world perish.<br /> <br /> 2. Baali<br /> They lack the centralized command structure of other clans, but technically speaking they do have the ability to unleash greater demons on the planet baked into their clan discipline, so no need to learn magic or setup networks. One Baali just level grinds the XP and diablerizes their way to the right generation and the world dies.<br /> <br /> 3. Tremere<br /> I could go on about the Pyramid clan structure, magically secure havens, dominate and auspex, and the fact they are universally hated and considered too useful to kill, but let's be real here. The Path of Conjuring, at level 2 allows you to make 55 gallon drums of the scariest chemical weapons known to man. Thus every tremere who learns two dots in the path is technically a WMD with a reload function. At level 3 you can make complex devices like modern cell phones or 1950s nukes.<br /> <br /> If you have level 5 Path of Conjuring and level 5 Dominate, you can make a fake living body, use dominate to directly control it, and use it to fight in daylight or do suicide missions where you jump out just before death. Basically PoC5 + D5 basically makes the combat from Altered Carbon a reality for your character. Even if you kill the Tremere, you are never sure if you killed them for good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T03:05:06-07:00","id":1539092,"title":"","content":"I'll be boring and say they are all equally dangerous but in their own way. I certainly wouldn't want to end up on the bad side of any Cainite regardless of Clan since they all got a tool set for causing untold misery for you.<br /> <br /> So it probably comes down to what kind of misery and hurt scares you the most. Whatever it is, there's a Clan that can deliver it to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T11:00:26-07:00","id":1539106,"title":"","content":"The most dangerous clan is whatever the ST is interpreting while in a bad mood. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T11:38:19-07:00","id":1539107,"title":"","content":"I would say the Kiasyd<br /> Dominate, Necromancy, Kiasyd Alchemy, Abyss Mysticism, Obtenebration and Mytherceria... not to mention those ties to the Thallain?<br /> They easily could turn the world inside out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T14:16:27-07:00","id":1539112,"title":"","content":"My top 3:<br /> <br /> 1- <i><b>Dominate </b></i><b>Malkavian</b>: a clan whose individual members are well rounded dangers on every aspect. Obfuscate and the overall opinion on the clan means you'll usually get away with almost anything you do. And what you can do is to find each and every secret you want about anyone and anything, plus mess with their minds with extreme finesse.<br /> <br /> Since anyone can develop Physical Disciplines without a teacher or someone else's blood, you can develop this extra set of tools as you wish.<br /> <br /> 2- <b>Tremere/Giovanni</b>: pure access to power. Any clan with access to some sorcery, Necromancy, whatever, has a hell of a tool at their disposal. Individuals have a versatile array of options to either excell at one form of danger or cover a lot of different approaches. The clan as a whole has all the variety and power as agents.<br /> <br /> Tremere and Giovanni both take the lead by having the biggest arsenal of their respective arts and being extremely organized as a whole to use their assets to maximum effect.<br /> <br /> 3- <b>Nosferatu</b>: as a clan, they're the most organized information brokers around, and the most disciplined in using their arsenal to maximum effect, while their own secrets are made particularly hard to find as they literally bury themselves and their havens beyond the reach of most others.<br /> <br /> Simply there's no clan effectively more powerful. They're the power behind every throne and no one can have the luxury of being their enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T17:24:32-07:00","id":1539120,"title":"","content":"Which clan is the most &quot;dangerous&quot; is nebulous in my opinion, as there are many ways that can be interpreted. All clans are extremely dangerous in their own ways, and all clans have their own weaknesses and limitations. So I am going to respond with which clan I would least want to have as the Clan Enmity flaw for my PC (regardless of what kind of PC it is). (I am also writing from a pre-V5 perspective since I don't follow that.)<br /> <br /> 1) Tremere. They have access to a lot of different powers and are very organized. It'll be hard for any individual character to withstand that in a city.<br /> <br /> 2) Malkavians. Less because they are actually all that powerful, but because who knows how each one may attempt to screw with you. Hard to defend against things you'll never guess that are coming.<br /> <br /> 3) Ventrue. Hard to settle on the third option as there are many good candidates. Ultimately I decided on Ventrue because they are also extremely well organized, are masters of Dominate and Presence, and have a lot of influence and control in both mortal and vampire societies. In most domains they are going to make things very hard for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T00:33:11-07:00","id":1539132,"title":"","content":"Dangerous to my character, short run or long run : any clan from which you cannot defend yourself or take countermeasures.<br /> I put on top Tremere and/or Malkavian.<br /> Auspex will screw you every time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T16:03:06-07:00","id":1539172,"title":"","content":"Auspex, Obfuscate and Dominate or Presence can really screw with you big time and I could add the Tzismce Visscuide Discipline as a horrible bonus for fearsome kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-24-2024, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T15:47:12-07:00","id":1539259,"title":"","content":"If I was going with clans that could be scary then that would be the Hecate as there Necromancy powers to call up ghosts to haunt you, spy on you or learn things that you don't want known would give many pause and the Tzsimce Vissciude Discipline to reshape your flesh like clay and turn you into a nearly mindless monster or part of the Catherdal of Flesh would be a awful fate to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T16:34:40-07:00","id":1539270,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go with Toreador. I know they don't have the cool powers of some of the other groups, but I've always found the idea of the darkly &quot;artistic&quot; antitribu pretty terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T17:43:33-07:00","id":1539275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1539270#post1539270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to go with Toreador. I know they don't have the cool powers of some of the other groups, but I've always found the idea of the darkly &quot;artistic&quot; antitribu pretty terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes creativity is the scariest superpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T13:05:37-07:00","id":1539494,"title":"","content":"Or a bored Lasombra or Fiend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T16:36:38-07:00","id":1539507,"title":"","content":"On a macro level, probably the Ventrue for how many mortal institutions they have their fingers in. But for specific regions this would change to whatever the dominant clan in the area is.<br /> <br /> On a personal level, the Malkavians for the sheer unpredictability. Proper preparation can defend against or avoid most threats, but how do you prepare for threats that you can't can't understand or even conceive of?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T12:52:14-07:00","id":1539549,"title":"","content":"Indeed the Malkavians and Ravnos ability to screw with your sense of reality shouldn't be overlooked and the Tzismce discipline of reshaping your flesh like clay is another level of horror when you think about it Matt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T23:24:37-07:00","id":1539577,"title":"","content":"Caitiff :&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T01:56:10-07:00","id":1539580,"title":"","content":"The core seven.<br /> <br /> I was originally going to do the old 'none, they're dangerous in different ways', but I think there's a difference between the original seven Clans and the subsequent additions, and that's the power sets. The lack of specialty disciplines gives them broad but practical abilities.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra are about projecting power, as a blunt hammer of necessary. The Venture are about projecting power you can't get rid of. While the Brujah are physical powerhouses their words are also ones which change the world. The Toreador's eyes let them build beauty, but also tear down both it and you.<br /> <br /> The original seven have three/four clans set up to find your every secret and hold them over you. As well as four that can break you down with their words, and three that'll mess you up physically. Then you have the Gangrel, who just won't die.<br /> <br /> Out of all of them the Tremere edge the others out just slightly, but only because you have no clue what powers they might pull out of their hat.<br /> <br /> There's a reason these seven were reworked into the Requiem Clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T22:43:20-07:00","id":1539677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1539580#post1539580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core seven.<br /> <br /> I was originally going to do the old 'none, they're dangerous in different ways', but I think there's a difference between the original seven Clans and the subsequent additions, and that's the power sets. The lack of specialty disciplines gives them broad but practical abilities.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra are about projecting power, as a blunt hammer of necessary. The Venture are about projecting power you can't get rid of. While the Brujah are physical powerhouses their words are also ones which change the world. The Toreador's eyes let them build beauty, but also tear down both it and you.<br /> <br /> The original seven have three/four clans set up to find your every secret and hold them over you. As well as four that can break you down with their words, and three that'll mess you up physically. Then you have the Gangrel, who just won't die.<br /> <br /> Out of all of them the Tremere edge the others out just slightly, but only because you have no clue what powers they might pull out of their hat.<br /> <br /> There's a reason these seven were reworked into the Requiem Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. In general I find the common Disciplines more valuable than the unique ones, giving advantage to the Camarilla clans. I'm not sure about the Lasombra: Obtenebration is cool, but I'm not sure I would choose it over a common discipline.<br /> <br /> That said, if rules and editions are taken into account, some things work out weaker or stronger than one might expect. Ex.: VDA20 Presence and Serpentis.<br /> Serpentis is extremely strong for fighters, and Warriors of Glycon have Potence in-clan. I would fear a Setite enclave having mighty warriors and leaders (Warriors of Glycon), dangerous and effective intellectuals and preachers (Priests), and tricky Witches of Echidna with Thaumaturgy. They can threaten people from any direction (social, mental, physical, mystical) with a brutal effectiveness matched only maybe by Assamites, as they also have 3 castes. But Quietus Cruscitus is not as good as Serpentis for fighting in my opinion, and Quietus Hematus is not as useful as other disciplines. And Setites of all 3 VDA20 bloodlines are much more likely to have plenty of goons and cultists around them than Assamites.<br /> Presence, on the other side, if one rules that spending 1 willpower point and passing a Willpower test at difficulty 8 is sufficient to be protected from it for one scene, is extremely ineffective, as anyone with Willpower 5+ on average will pass the test. That weakens all the clans with Presence, even if lore wise Presence works more consistently and actually allows one to control emotions enough to make vampires the seductive and frightening menace that they are. <br /> <br /> This is mainly a lore vs rules thing. Had I written the lore based on these rules, the lore would have been different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T10:01:41-07:00","id":1539708,"title":"","content":"I believe that Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate, Presence and Protean make for a very formidable challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T10:32:48-07:00","id":1539710,"title":"","content":"It depends on how you look at it, I guess. I mean, if your fear is being beaten up in the street or shot, the Brujah and Gangrel clans would be the most dangerous, and although I think the Gangrel are stronger individually, the Brujah probably have the advantage in numbers. Now, the Ventrue clan generally has well-connected members with greater purchasing power, and if money is power, then they would be the most powerful and most capable of pulling a trick out of a hat. Now, if information is power, then we turn our attention to the Nosferatu. In addition to all this, we have other factors such as magic, member qualities, disciplines, goals, and even the unpredictability of the clan. That said, I think the top 3 would be like this:<br /> <br /> For common humans:<br /> 1. Brujah<br /> 2. Gangrel<br /> 3. Malkav<br /> <br /> For wealthier humans:<br /> 1. Ventrue<br /> 2. Lasombra<br /> 3. Assamite<br /> <br /> For other kindred:<br /> 1. Nosferatu<br /> 2. Ventrue or Lasombra<br /> 3. Assamite or Tremere<br /> <br /> For Garou and other species as a general rule:<br /> 1. Ventrue<br /> 2. Tzimice<br /> 3. Brujah","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T10:53:48-07:00","id":1539711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1539577#post1539577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caitiff :&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>They get into that business where each case is different, because they don't have the best no-life expectancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T20:53:36-07:00","id":1539734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1539710#post1539710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Garou and other species as a general rule:<br /> 1. Ventrue<br /> 2. Tzimice<br /> 3. Brujah</div> </div> </div> </div>I would put Assamite on this list instead of Brujah, if for no other reason than the fact that anti-material rifles exist and Quietus/Obfuscate make for very interesting hunting options. The distance negates most of the combat advantages of Garou and as long as you only do a single shot per encounter, they can't really track you. Plus, if they go into hiding, then you just start sniping the kin-folk until the come back out.<br /> <br /> Mages are human levels of squishy if they are not prepared, which once again means a sniper, ambush explosive trap, or poison works very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T06:20:31-07:00","id":1539747,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day advanced technology/technocratic magic edges out everybody bar mages in terms of pure lethality. Even mages aren't exactly going to beat the sleeping tiger even if the Traditions and Technocracy join together, they just have a lot more flexibility than makes them hard to predict on an individual level.<br /> <br /> Remember what eventually took down [Ravnos] wasn't done grand feat of magic, it was the Technocracy using technology mortals are completely capable of doing themselves, even if the cost of giant orbital mirrors would be prohibitive.<br /> <br /> Which then starts getting us into 'the best way to build a combat character is to make a social character and convince someone else to fight for you' territory. Which will always boil down to the Venture being the most dangerous (they have incredible charisma, mind control, AND tons of disposable income), followed by other leader-archetype clans, but that's nowhere near as fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T10:26:34-07:00","id":1539756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1539747#post1539747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day advanced technology/technocratic magic edges out everybody bar mages in terms of pure lethality. Even mages aren't exactly going to beat the sleeping tiger even if the Traditions and Technocracy join together, they just have a lot more flexibility than makes them hard to predict on an individual level.<br /> <br /> Remember what eventually took down [Ravnos] wasn't done grand feat of magic, it was the Technocracy using technology mortals are completely capable of doing themselves, even if the cost of giant orbital mirrors would be prohibitive.<br /> <br /> Which then starts getting us into 'the best way to build a combat character is to make a social character and convince someone else to fight for you' territory. Which will always boil down to the Venture being the most dangerous (they have incredible charisma, mind control, AND tons of disposable income), followed by other leader-archetype clans, but that's nowhere near as fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the reflection on the relationship between social and physical play. Quite true.<br /> <br /> That works though because the player/ST still has to come up with the plan, rather than the PC/NPC, in reality. If that was accounted for, mental characters (with high Willpower too, not just mental Attributes) would be the ones who come up with plans and a way to convince some social character to do the work for them, who in turn recruit the muscle.<br /> Charm and money alone don't work if you can't outsmart someone better at planning and exploiting shortcomings than you. You'll just end up being unknowingly a pawn on their chessboard.<br /> <br /> Luckily (kind of) for the denizens of WoD, it seems like NPCs' intelligence and perceptiveness is always directly proportional to their insanity in one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T10:49:21-07:00","id":1539758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1539747#post1539747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which then starts getting us into 'the best way to build a combat character is to make a social character and convince someone else to fight for you' territory. Which will always boil down to the Venture being the most dangerous (they have incredible charisma, mind control, AND tons of disposable income), followed by other leader-archetype clans, but that's nowhere near as fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Ventrue has Dominate and Presence, but practically every vampire has the ability to Blood Bond so Dominate and Presence are less auto-win buttons and more quality-of-life enhancements. I guess the question becomes who would be the best <u><i><b>defensive</b></i></u> social build which in turn uses Resources, Influence, and Minions to attack from a distance? Because I do consider that play style more fun than cracking skulls.<br /> <br /> In some of the games I have run, the most dangerous character ended up being a Tremere with Path of Technomancy, three dots in Dominate, and a ton of Background dots. They resided in a secure private chantry with a live in Herd, they used hacking and Resources to cripple cities or countries depending on their needs. A prince in a different city can't exactly do much if the Tremere never physically goes to their territory. The local Garou can't exactly do much if the local government rezones their ancestral lands to be a parking lot for a strip mall.<br /> <br /> I know that &quot;The Lost Boys&quot; street level game play is classical VtM play, but winning before the battle ever begins is more classical for being a Vampire regardless of system or genre.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T10:52:07-07:00","id":1539759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1539756#post1539756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the reflection on the relationship between social and physical play. Quite true.<br /> <br /> That works though because the player/ST still has to come up with the plan, rather than the PC/NPC, in reality. If that was accounted for, mental characters (with high Willpower too, not just mental Attributes) would be the ones who come up with plans and a way to convince some social character to do the work for them, who in turn recruit the muscle.<br /> Charm and money alone don't work if you can't outsmart someone better at planning and exploiting shortcomings than you. You'll just end up being unknowingly a pawn on their chessboard.<br /> <br /> Luckily (kind of) for the denizens of WoD, it seems like NPCs' intelligence and perceptiveness is always directly proportional to their insanity in one way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's easy to spin it the other way: sufficiently powerful social characters can outsource muscle, thinking, and anything else to other characters. Who needs to plan when you have a guy who can do that for you?<br /> <br /> Yes <i>in-play</i> a player still has to come up with The Plan. But fiction wise it can verily easily become 'social guy decides on The Goal, convinces a couple of mental guys to come up with The Plan and The Equipment, and then the physical guys enact The Plan's.<br /> <br /> Few characters can outsource like a social character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T12:09:42-07:00","id":1539761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1539759#post1539759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's easy to spin it the other way: sufficiently powerful social characters can outsource muscle, thinking, and anything else to other characters. Who needs to plan when you have a guy who can do that for you?<br /> <br /> Yes <i>in-play</i> a player still has to come up with The Plan. But fiction wise it can verily easily become 'social guy decides on The Goal, convinces a couple of mental guys to come up with The Plan and The Equipment, and then the physical guys enact The Plan's.<br /> <br /> Few characters can outsource like a social character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I chose the wrong word with &quot;planning&quot;. <br /> <br /> The mental character provides both a vision for a worthy goal and a route towards it, and he does not need to humble himself to anyone else in the pursuit of his plan except as a pretense for convenience. A less smart character will pursue proportionately less worthwhile goals, easily made irrelevant even if attained, and will need to submit to the lead of the smart people to whom he outsources the planning. Human or vampire, nobody likes to admit they're not smart enough to decide what to aim for or how to reach it, and that they have to submit to another's lead and planning in order to reach their goal, becoming a pawn in their own game. And even if they're sufficiently self-aware to actually listen and obey those to whom they have outsourced the planning, nothing protects them from unknowingly being a pawn <i>in their plans.</i><br /> <br /> I am not talking about merely outsourcing some technical thing for which one lacks the specific skill or knowledge. That's normal. But you still have to be smart to play the game, above all. The smart person figures out easily how much social and physical might they need and where and how to source it from in the most effective and safest manner, while the social character outsources easily but doesn't see the full picture, and no amount of outsourcing can safely compensate that.<br /> <br /> Even rules wise, what the mental character lacks in social traits they can compensate by researching allies and opponents' hopes and fears and using leverage accordingly, translated in additional dice or lower difficulties. And once they have secured in this way the services of enough social characters, they're set to win.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T20:03:27-07:00","id":1539776,"title":"","content":"I can't see the Caitiff being considered a real danger as they tend to have a harder time learning there Disciplines and the clans keep under heel for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T22:41:19-07:00","id":1539780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1539776#post1539776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see the Caitiff being considered a real danger as they tend to have a harder time learning there Disciplines and the clans keep under heel for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few Caitif who caused problems along the line...<br /> Mukhtar Bey<br /> The Stoneman<br /> Osiris<br /> And don't forget the whole second Generation and Caine himself<br /> The <i>Clanless </i>could be very dangerous - even as Thin-bloods - under the right circumstances<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T08:50:09-07:00","id":1539791,"title":"","content":"True about the kindred you mentioned, but there more exceptions to the rule with the current crop of clanless and I can see the Thin Bloods being a potential threat as they do have advantages over the rest and the Book of Nod do talk about them .<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T12:15:37-07:00","id":1539795,"title":"","content":"I think the whole &quot;technology is more dangerous&quot; approach misses context badly.<br /> <br /> Technology isn't something you can have at hand all the time, in all its forms, to do anything you please without consequence. There's only so much you can carry on your person casually without bringing the wrong attention, even in the US.<br /> <br /> About the Caitiff... I wouldn't say they're the most dangerous because they don't have a reliable power set (PCs may have, &quot;average&quot; Caitiff do not). But they are serious contenders, as they're unpredictable.<br /> <br /> Being able to develop any power, even ones that should be out of reach, plus completely new ones, that's a scary level of versatility that can produce unimaginably powerful individuals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T13:59:19-07:00","id":1539801,"title":"","content":"Banu Haqim are more versatile with their sorcery so they're objectively more dangerous, but running into a City Gangrel in a cramped alley when you're not expecting to would imo be WAY scarier to deal with.<br /> <br /> If I'm some random stressed-out neonate and I finally meet a cat that doesn't hiss and run away from me, I don't think I'd notice its not breathing or blinking until I'm already trying to pet it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28284-abugintherug","name":"abugintherug","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28284_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T19:10:18-07:00","id":1539813,"title":"","content":"The Banu Haqim are quite formidable with there skills and Disciplines, but having a Gangrel after you or having a Malkavian or Ravnos messing with you from directions you wouldn't predict or even an elder Caitiff with unusual wildcard abilities can make for a more dangerous threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T08:32:41-07:00","id":1540843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1539776#post1539776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see the Caitiff being considered a real danger as they tend to have a harder time learning there Disciplines and the clans keep under heel for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Caitiff are the most dangerous not because of anything they've ever really done, but because of the reaction of every other Cainite in the region just for them existing. If the vampire clans are a nest of hornets then a Caitiff just by existing, is the equivalent of hitting that nest with a stick. They're Harbingers of Gehenna though no fault of their own, and the chaos that gets sewn in the efforts to squash them has helped drive the Jyhad to extremes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T16:38:52-07:00","id":1540920,"title":"","content":"Caitiffs are the wildcard in the enternel struggles of the undead as it upsets there established order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T22:48:18-07:00","id":1541956,"title":"","content":"Banu Haqim.<br /> <br /> They can sneak up on you, and make your supernaturally fast murder absolutely silent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T21:26:50-07:00","id":1542443,"title":"","content":"Most???<br /> <br /> The one that's in the environment that suites them best while maligning the others the most. <br /> <br /> Venture wealth and Dominate don't mean much down in the sewers, for example?<br /> <br /> All vamps and clans are dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T01:39:12-07:00","id":1542449,"title":"","content":"Not sure who's the most dangerous, but Nosferatu are definitely the least dangerous. Nothing to see here mate, don't mind us ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25078-brickman","name":"Brickman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T12:09:40-07:00","id":1542489,"title":"","content":"The Nosferatu shouldn't be overlooked as a very serious threat as they have sharp ears and eyes with the use of Animalism and being able to hide themselves or bolt holes and look like others with use of the Obfuscate Discipline and for plain old intimidation value you can't go wrong with Potence. But as useful as they are, it's how they use the information they gain to ensure there safety Brickman and the rest of the clans know this quite well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T09:03:42-07:00","id":1542511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542489#post1542489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nosferatu shouldn't be overlooked as a very serious threat as they have sharp ears and eyes with the use of Animalism and being able to hide themselves or bolt holes and look like others with use of the Obfuscate Discipline and for plain old intimidation value you can't go wrong with Potence. But as useful as they are, it's how they use the information they gain to ensure there safety Brickman and the rest of the clans know this quite well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nosferatu Obfuscate is so powerful, everyone forgets how dangerous they can get...<br /> <br /> How many Nos signature characters are there? Everyone has their Lucita waifu fantasies. Obfuscate prevents that kind of attention.<br /> <br /> Nos, along with Gangrel, Lasombra, and to a lesser extent Setites and Tremere, are just a notch under the Assamites as far as assassins. IMO, Assamites are a bit wasteful. Nos(and Gangrel) are better at Infiltration than the Assamites. Nos smoke the Assamites in Arson. And Animalism clans can attrit non-Animalism clans which is why they usually hang outside the city, or at the borders - ive used this in DA games. <br /> <br /> Nos discipline spread is very cost efficient in V20. Compare to Celerity and Quietus which are pretty costly blood-wise. Same with Brujah and Celerity+Potence.<br /> <br /> Nos Boogeyman can abduct someone(Potence to easily carry a subdued person) and take them deep down below - think that movie Aliens with the colonists glued to the walls with eggs implanted in their chest. Think about it: a strong enough Obfuscate4 and Potence could let a Nos just...nab someone in a group and disappear them and the group would be left wondering if that person slipped off to the restroom.<br /> <br /> <br /> Leatherface serial murderers and arsonists. Wassail or not? Coterie gets to find out! <br /> <br /> <br /> Local disease outbreaks. Oh, yeah, local drug outbreaks in a city <i>must</i> be the Setites. <br /> <br /> <br /> Obfuscate+Animalism5 utterly <b><i>RUINS</i></b> plots and NPCs(less so in the Sabbat, but still).&quot;Shame about X, she keeps losing it at Elysium. Prince is gonna have to do something about that. The Curse can be difficult for some, after all. I wonder whats gonna happen to her turf? And she owes that rather large Boon to Y. Y better get payment soon.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nos racket #1: Obfuscate3 and mask as Vamp Y. Diddle Vamp X's ghoul while masked as Y. Start shit between X and Y. Sell info to either or both X and Y. Profit.<br /> <br /> Nos Racket #2: Find struggling Neonate. Become his friend and offer support(feeding/friendship/haven/etc). Help establish that Vamp. Set up scenarios to help that vamp get Boons over other NPCs(see racket #1). Profit from Proxy-Boons. Bonus if local Elders do 'Horse-Trading' with Boons. Its a dirty game, after all...<br /> <br /> Nos racket #3: Lies, damned Lies, Statistics, and Countermeasures. Nos info is reliable, everyone knows! Dont believe? Ask the Dominate-using Primogen, he will verify Nos X tells the truth! Because Nos X saw the (obfuscated by another Nos)truth with his own eyes! Keeping some Broodmates in the dark has some advantages!<br /> <br /> <br /> Vid on YouTube: SABBAT PACKS HATE WHEN YOU SHARE THIS ONE EASY AGGRAVTED DAMAGE TRICK!!! COMBAT WILL NEVER BE THE SAME!<br /> <br /> Some decades ago, my friends did some math on Revised Combat. I dont remember the details but idea goes: once a Char can deliver 4 Aggra damage/per attack, anything more is pretty much wasted. Even 3 is a lot. Delivery of that damage becomes the bigger factor. Everyone forgets every vamp can do Aggra damage with a Grapple+Bite. But few vamps have the dice pools to do so easily and reliably. So which dice pools facilitate the easiest delivery?<br /> <br /> Now, once <i>could </i>invest tons of XP in Disciplines like Quietus(poorly written in V20 and a waste past lvl2), Lure of Flames, or high level Combo powers like that Brujah flaming-fist one.<br /> <br /> OR THIS THIS ONE SIMPLE TRICK...<br /> <br /> Have the shop skills to take a $15 machete, drill holes in it, dip in Tar/other sticky viscous flammable material, and have a cheap flaming sword. Be sure to wear your leathers while using.<br /> Which Clan will tend to have more members that have basic Shop skills? The one that lives in scrap heaps? So, a Nos with Dex2+melee2 using a machete(S+1?) and Str2 + Potence2 will usually net 1-2 successes to hit vs non-elite opponents and for 1BP/turn do 5-6 damage per single attack with 2 of that damage guaranteed. Fortitude5 nets 2.5 successes on average. It gets dumber if you think about using Athletics.<br /> <br /> Incendiary sniper rifle headshots are the other avenue but that favors Malkavians and Toreadors.<br /> <br /> Lasombra Tentacle King keeping you down? They get squeamish when a Nos with a Flaregun walks into the room. Monomancy Trials get interesting if ST remembers Nos and Gangrel may have Animalism5.<br /> <br /> All in all, you cant blame people for sleeping on Nosferatu as being helpless. They cant see through Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T03:51:21-07:00","id":1542542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542511#post1542511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nos racket #1: Obfuscate3 and mask as Vamp Y. Diddle Vamp X's ghoul while masked as Y. Start shit between X and Y. Sell info to either or both X and Y. Profit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Requires 3 or 4 success on a roll with Difficulty 7, and likely several points of blood to to make up for the difference in appearance.<br /> <br /> Also fails if someone has enough Auspex (one of the most common disciplines) or if you get caught on camera ...<br /> <br /> Obfluscate is powerfull in theory but in praxis it is just not that reliable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T17:27:41-07:00","id":1542596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542542#post1542542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requires 3 or 4 success on a roll with Difficulty 7, and likely several points of blood to to make up for the difference in appearance.<br /> <br /> Also fails if someone has enough Auspex (one of the most common disciplines) or if you get caught on camera ...<br /> <br /> Obfluscate is powerfull in theory but in praxis it is just not that reliable.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>YMMV but in my experience most Nos prioritize Obfuscate and few Auspex clans prioritize Auspex over other Disciplines. <br /> <br /> It's a white room counter that people don't factor in the XP needed for PCs or how many NPCs will have Auspex 3+. Obfuscate = Auspex is a contested roll and Nos tend to live by those skills rather then dabble in them. With planning, the blood is a minimal factor.<br /> <br /> It's not like some newb Nos with a 4 dice pool will try to pull this off with any proficiency. A lot of the Nos tricks are gonna require skill and planning. And they likely won't be trying that ploy every night. <br /> <br /> Cameras? Well, there's a Nos Merit for that, which I don't see why and modern player wouldn't take it. Very strong without being OP, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T18:50:46-07:00","id":1542654,"title":"","content":"I'd say the only clan that even gives equal weight to Auspex as their other disciplines is the Malkavians, and I doubt shit-stirring Nosferatu try to fool them much as their reactions can be so unpredictable and, well, just leaving them alone to do their own thing will probably result in as much shit being stirred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T19:40:07-07:00","id":1542658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542596#post1542596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not like some newb Nos with a 4 dice pool will try to pull this off with any proficiency. A lot of the Nos tricks are gonna require skill and planning. And they likely won't be trying that ploy every night.<br /> <br /> Cameras? Well, there's a Nos Merit for that, which I don't see why and modern player wouldn't take it. Very strong without being OP, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>While your points are valid for a PC Nos, the problem here is that you must apply the same assumptions to Nos as to other clans, and you\u2019re clearly not doing it.<br /> <br /> Any merit is a rare ability to begin with. It can be cheap or just too beneficial for a player not to get it, but that\u2019s because <b>players</b> buy Merits. <b>Characters</b> don\u2019t, they either have it or not. And every Merit is, again, rare by definition.<br /> <br /> The frequency of Auspex X to Obfuscate X doesn\u2019t have all that of a weight, either. For using this setup as a reliable strategy, the risk is too much. Surely it is a thing you can do if and when you\u2019re certain about how vulnerable your victim is. Otherwise, though, it\u2019s asking to eventually fail hard, and the one time you fail will already be a big problem.<br /> <br /> Finally, the very Nos culture plays against this. The Nos rely heavily on their reputation for good information. If they start to be caught fabricating shit here and there, that\u2019s a very big problem. And hence Obfuscate isn\u2019t an unknown power, sloppy or frequent use of this strategy is enough to tip others on it even if no one gets you with Auspex.<br /> <br /> Overall that\u2019s a very hamfisted and sloppy use of Obfuscate if used in the way you described, and unlikely to nearly play as well as it apparently does in your games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T23:07:26-07:00","id":1542667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542658#post1542658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While your points are valid for a PC Nos, the problem here is that you must apply the same assumptions to Nos as to other clans, and you\u2019re clearly not doing it.<br /> <br /> Any merit is a rare ability to begin with. It can be cheap or just too beneficial for a player not to get it, but that\u2019s because <b>players</b> buy Merits. <b>Characters</b> don\u2019t, they either have it or not. And every Merit is, again, rare by definition.<br /> <br /> The frequency of Auspex X to Obfuscate X doesn\u2019t have all that of a weight, either. For using this setup as a reliable strategy, the risk is too much. Surely it is a thing you can do if and when you\u2019re certain about how vulnerable your victim is. Otherwise, though, it\u2019s asking to eventually fail hard, and the one time you fail will already be a big problem.<br /> <br /> Finally, the very Nos culture plays against this. The Nos rely heavily on their reputation for good information. If they start to be caught fabricating shit here and there, that\u2019s a very big problem. And hence Obfuscate isn\u2019t an unknown power, sloppy or frequent use of this strategy is enough to tip others on it even if no one gets you with Auspex.<br /> <br /> Overall that\u2019s a very hamfisted and sloppy use of Obfuscate if used in the way you described, and unlikely to nearly play as well as it apparently does in your games.</div> </div> </div> </div>How am i not applying it to other clans? Not sure what you mean.<br /> <br /> Merits as rare? Our STs felt free to add them to NPCs to spice them up. Pre...i want to say Revised, there werent Merits so we were familiar with that Merit-less as well. &quot;rare&quot; is subjective in this case i would think. We started using them more and more after Revised, partly to MinMax chargen, partly for something different. <br /> <br /> Frequency of Auspex to Obfuscate? Gonna depend on Edition, if i remember Earlier editions NPCs had a lot of rare out of clan disciplines. That evened-out by Revised? But going on memory - i could be wrong- but if you tallied up all the NPCs in the 'by Night' books, i would bet average Auspex was lower than average Nos Obfuscate, Elders being the likely exception.<br /> <br /> Now at our tables, Discipline spreads were based on char concept and the clan survival strategy. <br /> <br /> All the games you played at all the tables: how many Fortitude only Ventrue/Gangrel were there? Auspex only Toreador/Tremere(specially Tremere)? Animalism only Tzimisce? Celerity only Assamites? Potence only Giovanni/Brujah(these may be more concept fitting btw)? <br /> <br /> Risk? Thats a naive take. You act like vampires dont have Beasts, ambitions, or desire for power just to survive. Ever play the boardgame Diplomacy? Someone ALWAYS gets fucked, the lesson of that game is dont be that person, and if you want to win you will be screwing just the right person at just the right time. Ever play Poker? Take too little risk, you lose. And some Poker players on some hands assume LOTS of risk on a bluff and it works often enough to be viable. <br /> <br /> Nosferatu culture? Again a na\u00efve take. Maybe Nos at your tables are too scared of their own shadows to risk tarnishing their reputations. At our tables, Nos can be just as ambitious as any powermonger Ventrue or Tremere. As catty and vengeful as any Toreador or Brujah. As crazy as any Malkavian. As subversive as any Setite, etc. One of the Nosferatu character archetypes is called a 'Leatherface', literally a serial murderer...what about its reputation? The Clan's for not putting those guys down?<br /> <br /> Apply that logic to the Tremere and how they stole immortality. Kinda risky pissing of some 3rd Gen Vamp, yes? They did it anyway. And it worked. It may be falling apart in current Lore but howm many PCs actually play dealing with that fallout? probably not many.<br /> <br /> Sloppy Obfuscate? If you say so. I even said they wouldnt likely try it very often. Its a viable strat that can work, and can make memorable play. like a Tremere boosting his Generation to Dominate an Elder, etc. A Setite trying to get the heart of some desperate and powerful Elder. A Toreador trying to mindread an Elder at Elysium. Ever try anything wild like that? or do all your chars stick to boring fetch-quests and seducing potential ghouls?<br /> <br /> In our games stuff like this usually plays well: if it works, its memorable and fun. if it doesnt work, its memorable and fun. Hamfisted? Maybe. Or maybe your tables are boring?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T23:18:13-07:00","id":1542668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542654#post1542654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the only clan that even gives equal weight to Auspex as their other disciplines is the Malkavians, and I doubt shit-stirring Nosferatu try to fool them much as their reactions can be so unpredictable and, well, just leaving them alone to do their own thing will probably result in as much shit being stirred.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree, and Cappadocians in DA? Equal weight, or even investing heavily/exclusively in Auspex.<br /> <br /> I would say in general, Malkavians have some advantage over Nosferatu if they werent so distracted and lacking potence/celerity. They can be pretty oblique, like the Tremere. That clan is pretty ST dependent, but the Malk Discipline spread is pretty favorable to dealing with Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspec