Giovanni/Brujah(these may be more concept fitting btw)?<br /> <br /> Risk? Thats a naive take. You act like vampires dont have Beasts, ambitions, or desire for power just to survive. Ever play the boardgame Diplomacy? Someone ALWAYS gets fucked, the lesson of that game is dont be that person, and if you want to win you will be screwing just the right person at just the right time. Ever play Poker? Take too little risk, you lose. And some Poker players on some hands assume LOTS of risk on a bluff and it works often enough to be viable.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu culture? Again a na\u00efve take. Maybe Nos at your tables are too scared of their own shadows to risk tarnishing their reputations. At our tables, Nos can be just as ambitious as any powermonger Ventrue or Tremere. As catty and vengeful as any Toreador or Brujah. As crazy as any Malkavian. As subversive as any Setite, etc. One of the Nosferatu character archetypes is called a 'Leatherface', literally a serial murderer...what about its reputation? The Clan's for not putting those guys down?<br /> <br /> Apply that logic to the Tremere and how they stole immortality. Kinda risky pissing of some 3rd Gen Vamp, yes? They did it anyway. And it worked. It may be falling apart in current Lore but howm many PCs actually play dealing with that fallout? probably not many.<br /> <br /> Sloppy Obfuscate? If you say so. I even said they wouldnt likely try it very often. Its a viable strat that can work, and can make memorable play. like a Tremere boosting his Generation to Dominate an Elder, etc. A Setite trying to get the heart of some desperate and powerful Elder. A Toreador trying to mindread an Elder at Elysium. Ever try anything wild like that? or do all your chars stick to boring fetch-quests and seducing potential ghouls?<br /> <br /> In our games stuff like this usually plays well: if it works, its memorable and fun. if it doesnt work, its memorable and fun. Hamfisted? Maybe. Or maybe your tables are boring?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey buddy, what an arrogant and aggressively unnecessary response. Everyone here is a narrator and player with some level of experience playing Vampire the Masquerade, exchanging ideas. You should get down from this level of arrogance and superiority. No one here asked if your game table has super players with super vampire genius conspirators in their super chronicle.<br /> <br /> Be more respectful of ideas that differ from yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T07:40:26-07:00","id":1542684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542680#post1542680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey buddy, what an arrogant and aggressively unnecessary response. Everyone here is a narrator and player with some level of experience playing Vampire the Masquerade, exchanging ideas. You should get down from this level of arrogance and superiority. No one here asked if your game table has super players with super vampire genius conspirators in their super chronicle.<br /> <br /> Be more respectful of ideas that differ from yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>I reply in-kind, Mr. Respecfulness-police.<br /> <br /> Where was i arrogant? <br /> <br /> You are right, everyone here is a narrator and player. Why didnt you levy this allegation against the person i responded to who called my interpretation &quot;hamfisted&quot;, &quot;sloppy&quot;, and &quot;not likely to work well&quot; outside my tables, which is essentially a &quot;your fun is wrong&quot; argument. What about your concern of their &quot;level of arrogance and superiority&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T08:29:52-07:00","id":1542689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542684#post1542684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I reply in-kind, Mr. Respecfulness-police.<br /> <br /> Where was i arrogant?<br /> <br /> You are right, everyone here is a narrator and player. Why didnt you levy this allegation against the person i responded to who called my interpretation &quot;hamfisted&quot;, &quot;sloppy&quot;, and &quot;not likely to work well&quot; outside my tables, which is essentially a &quot;your fun is wrong&quot; argument. What about your concern of their &quot;level of arrogance and superiority&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I refer to you as buddy, I respect you.<br /> <br /> When you call me Mr. Respectfulness-police, you are just trying to offend with your irony.<br /> <br /> When Monteparnas writes sloppily, he is not trying to insult or offend you. He is saying that there are more efficient ways to use discipline. He is not imposing a correct way to play. He is just describing that there may be more efficient and less risky ways to use discipline.<br /> <br /> You saying that his game is boring just because he has a different view than yours is simply arrogant. At no point did he question your ability as a storyteller or how your game table is run, unlike you, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T12:37:33-07:00","id":1542710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542596#post1542596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like some newb Nos with a 4 dice pool will try to pull this off with any proficiency. A lot of the Nos tricks are gonna require skill and planning. And they likely won't be trying that ploy every night.</div> </div> </div> </div>But for the needed 3 or 4 success against difficulty 7 pretty much need a maxed out sice pool and even than it isn't really a sure thing.<br /> <br /> You can certainly build a character that can pull it of, but the average Nosferatu will not be able to do that.<br /> <br /> And when it comes to Auspex, sure most Vampires don't have it, but the really important ones often have.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T22:50:01-07:00","id":1542751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542684#post1542684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I reply in-kind, Mr. Respecfulness-police.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Please refrain from being disrespectful to other users and their tables. See Rule 1. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T23:07:51-07:00","id":1542753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542689#post1542689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I refer to you as buddy, I respect you.<br /> <br /> When you call me Mr. Respectfulness-police, you are just trying to offend with your irony.<br /> <br /> When Monteparnas writes sloppily, he is not trying to insult or offend you. He is saying that there are more efficient ways to use discipline. He is not imposing a correct way to play. He is just describing that there may be more efficient and less risky ways to use discipline.<br /> <br /> You saying that his game is boring just because he has a different view than yours is simply arrogant. At no point did he question your ability as a storyteller or how your game table is run, unlike you, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Buddy' can be used in a condescending or a friendly manner. How was i to know? But since you clarified, ill assume good intentions and take back my snarky comment.<br /> <br /> You claim Montepamas wasnt trying to offend, but he/she says my view is 'hamfisted and sloppy&quot; and likely wont work outside the table i play at. Pretty presumptuous. Ive seen such tactics at a few different tables with different groups over the years. <br /> <br /> Was i even speaking of efficiency in the first place?<br /> <br /> The boring comment WAS meant to be arrogant. Because its kinda arrogant to say my example of play would only work at tables i myself play at, yes? Montepamas didnt provide any mechanical examples of why it wouldnt work, only hand-waived claims of risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T23:23:04-07:00","id":1542754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542710#post1542710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for the needed 3 or 4 success against difficulty 7 pretty much need a maxed out since pool and even than it isn't really a sure thing.<br /> <br /> You can certainly build a character that can pull it of, but the average Nosferatu will not be able to do that.<br /> <br /> And when it comes to Auspex, sure most Vampires don't have it, but the really important ones often have.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maxxed pool, sure, or at least 8 dice, which can be obtained at chargen. +/- a WP spent.<br /> <br /> Average neonate, sure, not likely. Ancilla...may be closer to that pool than say the average vamp of another clan to one of their dice pools that support a single discipline power. Reasoning being Nos rely heavily upon Obfuscate, unless say they never mingle in public like a bestial type thats focuses on Animialism.<br /> <br /> Auspex, yeah sure. But are powerful Elders and Ancients commonly out and about in the world watching over the shoulders of all the other vamps to protect them from such obfuscate uses? I would be inclined to say not likely. Does the PC/NPC have the balls or skill to do such vs a way more powerful vamp? Thats a valid question, but one of Player agency and ST plot crafting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-27T11:59:10-07:00","id":1542789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542753#post1542753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> she says my view is 'hamfisted and sloppy&quot; and likely wont work outside the table i play at.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify context, this thread is about <i><b>clan</b></i>, not character. What I said, I said in this context. <b>In this context</b>, what you said seemed to be about the clan as a whole, instead of being sample strategies a particular character can follow.<br /> <br /> Regardless of that, I didn't dedicate my entire post to attack how I think you play, I gave my opinion on your arguments.<br /> <br /> Given the context, whatever you say about the Nosferatu, <b>I will take it as being suggestions for how the clan as a whole behaves</b>. Or there's simply no point.<br /> <br /> And the final &quot;apparently does in your table&quot; was to acknowledge that, had I understood correctly (hence &quot;apparently&quot;), then it does work at your table as described. Which is fine by me.<br /> <br /> It was not my intention to be aggressive, although I may not have expressed myself in the best way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T02:08:46-07:00","id":1542898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542754#post1542754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex, yeah sure. But are powerful Elders and Ancients commonly out and about in the world watching over the shoulders of all the other vamps to protect them from such obfuscate uses?</div> </div> </div> </div>No but there is usually pretty little to gain by screwing over other neonates.<br /> <br /> And allready with Ancialla (at least from Auspex Clans) there is a certain level of risk since you hardly ever know for sure how much Auspex they have ...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T08:22:17-07:00","id":1542908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542789#post1542789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To clarify context, this thread is about <i><b>clan</b></i>, not character. What I said, I said in this context. <b>In this context</b>, ...<br /> <br /> Given the context, whatever you say about the Nosferatu, <b>I will take it as being suggestions for how the clan as a whole behaves</b>. Or there's simply no point.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> It was not my intention to be aggressive, although I may not have expressed myself in the best way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, the context is the Clan, but clans are made of individuals that share similar Disciplines and more generally - skills. The Lore, Curse, and Discipline spread inform a context in which the average individual Nos is likely to operate. So while giving one example of play for one character can be less relevant overall, i would say that if the example is a tactic that suits a common environment that is available to all the clan members, in a clan that is far more inclined to share such tactics, then it may be more appropriate. Compare to say, a Tzimisce that develops some new Vicissitude tactic, may not share it at all due to competition within the clan in a clan that really doesnt promote teamwork.<br /> <br /> As far as your intentions, fair enough, ill take you at your word. If i come off aggressive, nothing personal is meant by it, my profession demands i be blunt and argue, and it has rubbed off on me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T08:30:48-07:00","id":1542909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542898#post1542898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No but there is usually pretty little to gain by screwing over other neonates.<br /> <br /> And allready with Ancialla (at least from Auspex Clans) there is a certain level of risk since you hardly ever know for sure how much Auspex they have ...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I see it less as 'screwing over', unless your char concept does that, and more... taking advantage of/grooming/positioning. Neonates dont generally have lots of power, unless you play small town, but they may grow in power and the more vamps dig into each other, it may bear fruit later. Hence the old saying: Coteries generally dont survive Age. <br /> <br /> Even true with the Ancilla, but risk can be managed, and some people are very good at it. <br /> <br /> Otherwise what would the VtM play experience be if all the vamps were too scared of risk to do anything? Imagine Ventrue that dont try to Dominate each other out of fear, or Toreador too scared to slide into the graces of the powerful and help themselves to some of that Cantillon Effect, or Brujah too scared to beat up some fool talking a counter ideology, or a Malkavian to scared to pull a prank the voices in his head are championing, or a Setite too scared to push that new cult...<br /> <br /> IMO, half the fun of this game is the risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T12:49:57-07:00","id":1542924,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sad that this discussion has become just, X Discipline vs X Discipline makes X Clan more dangerous. While they are surely a factor, they're only a minor part of what makes each Clan and Bloodline. Disciplines don't make a Vampire, and only the crudest and most inept solely rely on them to such an extent that its their whole world. The movers and shakers of the WoD hardly need powers to be a threat.<br /> <br /> I still say its the Caitiff though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T13:06:03-07:00","id":1542927,"title":"","content":"Disciplines make for useful tools, but they work best as an ace in the hole when things get really dicey such as lupines, hunters or worse things coming into your orbit and you wasted vitae on things that could have been done without there use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T14:04:38-07:00","id":1542933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542908#post1542908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in a clan that is far more inclined to share such tactics</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is where frequencies and averages play their parts.<br /> <br /> A PC Nos can be easily built to pull this off reliably. An average Nos, while expected to have the general skillset to do so, can\u2019t be expected to be so good, unless we\u2019re talking at least Ancillae. Here is where Merits being a rare thing in the setting is relevant, as you can\u2019t expect most Nos in the city to be able to fool security cameras, and so on.<br /> <br /> Shared tactics add the problem that this means regular use. If a tactic is possible, but only the most skilled in the clan would use it, then there\u2019s no reason to expect it to be shared.<br /> <br /> We know by how their clan culture is described what the shared tactics of the Nos are. They do use their Obfuscate to collect information, and they share this information among themselves. The Nosferatu are known as the main information brokers in the setting, and they certainly didn\u2019t got there by respecting people\u2019s privacy.<br /> <br /> That said, though, fabricated scenarios are far more delicate and potentially harmful to their business if someone is caught doing it. You need a lot of skill and risk taking to pull it off, the results aren\u2019t reliable, and being caught can not only result in harsh punishment, but would jeopardize the entire clan\u2019s thing in the city.<br /> <br /> It is, as I said earlier, a valid option for a PC, or even for an NPC with the right combination of skill, ambition and circumstance. But as a \u201creason to fear the clan\u201d, I highly doubt it would figure among their shared tactics, quite the opposite: they would discourage such behavior, so to not create needless problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542924#post1542924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sad that this discussion has become just, X Discipline vs X Discipline makes X Clan more dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if that were true, why be sad?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think anyone here really stopped just at their Discipline spreads. But that said, we\u2019re comparing clans, not character creation, and the Discipline Spread is an important definer of the clan, what kind of powers you can expect with any consistency from its members.<br /> <br /> Also, it is deeply linked to their cultures. Nosferatu are information brokers because of their mastery over Obfuscate and Animalism, Tremere need their Auspex to be effective mystics and literally trade on their Thaumaturgy, both Toreador and Brujah are socially imposing due to Presence, while the Ventrue codified extensive traditions on the use of Dominate.<br /> <br /> Those clans aren\u2019t solely defined by their Disciplines, and even clans that share Disciplines use them differently, but still a lot of the clan\u2019s culture filters down in which powers they have and how they use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T21:22:45-07:00","id":1542943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542924#post1542924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sad that this discussion has become just, X Discipline vs X Discipline makes X Clan more dangerous. ...<br /> <br /> I still say its the Caitiff though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its more than that, is those cool powers in the context of the Clan survival strategy and niche of how it uses its power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T22:04:51-07:00","id":1543049,"title":"","content":"I agree that Disciplines in the right hands make for a dangerous kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T05:47:57-07:00","id":1543092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542943#post1542943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think its more than that, is those cool powers in the context of the Clan survival strategy and niche of how it uses its power.</div> </div> </div> </div>If its about disciplines, then Tzimisce wins. That's it. Game over. The Eldest has infected a full 2/3 the Kindred population. He owns the entirety of the Sabbat, the Tremere, and anyone who has ever shared vitae with either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T06:27:48-07:00","id":1543094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543092#post1543092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If its about disciplines, then Tzimisce wins. That's it. Game over. The Eldest has infected a full 2/3 the Kindred population. He owns the entirety of the Sabbat, the Tremere, and anyone who has ever shared vitae with either.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the risk of being pedantic this isn't correct. [Tzimisce] and Clan Tzimisce are two different things, even if strongly connected. Thus just because [Tzimisce] is very powerful don't mean that its Clan is powerful. Double so because [Tzimisce] don't seem like the paternalistic kind to care much for its offspring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T11:27:57-07:00","id":1543112,"title":"","content":"Having power doesn't always equal the knowledge or wisdom to use it properly. Most smart kindred know when to use it and when not to use it and I seem to recall in one of the older books try to use it sparingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T16:50:41-07:00","id":1543169,"title":"","content":"To be fair Gurkal, I would say that most of the 3rd generation don't have much of a paternal feeling towards there direct childer or there clans in general outside of how useful or tasty they might be. I'd go with the Emperor of Earth in Warhammer 40K as he views all his Primary sons as tools much to the horror of the restored Roberto Guileman and not much of the way of parental love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T19:45:20-07:00","id":1543179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543169#post1543169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair Gurkal, I would say that most of the 3rd generation don't have much of a paternal feeling towards there direct childer or there clans in general outside of how useful or tasty they might be. I'd go with the Emperor of Earth in Warhammer 40K as he views all his Primary sons as tools much to the horror of the restored Roberto Guileman and not much of the way of parental love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely possible but I'm afraid I don't know 40k lore sufficiently to engage in a discussion regarding this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T20:44:56-07:00","id":1543180,"title":"","content":"I was making a comparison on how much like the 3rd generation kindred attitude towards their clans is much like the Emperor's view of his Primarch children. There's not much way in paternal affection in both cases though sometimes they have a bonding moment or two but nothing that is considered anything human.<br /> <br /> Going back to Tziscme outside of Dracon and possibly Lambach Ruthhaven, there antiduilvean isn't very paternal and I can see perhaps the others may not even feel that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T13:26:52-07:00","id":1543210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543094#post1543094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the risk of being pedantic this isn't correct. [Tzimisce] and Clan Tzimisce are two different things, even if strongly connected. Thus just because [Tzimisce] is very powerful don't mean that its Clan is powerful. Double so because [Tzimisce] don't seem like the paternalistic kind to care much for its offspring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if this comparison is fair, but Tzimice gives the impression that he was never human, even more than others from the third generation, and among them would be Set and Malkav. Just commenting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T14:41:39-07:00","id":1543213,"title":"","content":"Indeed the Tziscme seems to been more of detached mortal even before his embrace. But he seemed to have some sort of paternal fondness for Dracon and Lambach Ruthhaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T17:02:33-07:00","id":1543229,"title":"","content":"From what little I remember of him in Gehenna he must see them as toys or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T17:18:13-07:00","id":1543231,"title":"","content":"If I remember in regards to the Dracon, the antiduilvean did have some sort of parental feeling for his Childe and brought out some human element and respected him enough to decide to allow Dracon to choose to be embraced. With Ruthhaven it's not certain what he finds worthy to protect.<br /> <br /> In addition the eldest seemed to go out of his way to ensure Dracon survival when the shaper wanted to end it all after the fall of the Trinity. Though forcing his Childe to merge with Vykos might put a damper on any warm feelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T21:04:44-07:00","id":1543727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543094#post1543094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the risk of being pedantic this isn't correct. [Tzimisce] and Clan Tzimisce are two different things, even if strongly connected. Thus just because [Tzimisce] is very powerful don't mean that its Clan is powerful. Double so because [Tzimisce] don't seem like the paternalistic kind to care much for its offspring.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Tzimisce] <b><i>is</i></b> Clan Tzimisce. They are all just extensions of itself, more so than any other clan founder to its clan. Through its blood it became legion, rather than one being. It cares for its progeny like you care for individual skin cells. They do their thing, and if you lose a few here and there, who cares.<br /> <br /> The only other clan that comes close to Tzimisce are the Malkavians with the Malkavian Madness Network, but Malkav exerts for less control on his progeny, where [Tzimisce] can and will manifest through any of them if it feels like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T22:21:55-07:00","id":1543731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543727#post1543727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [Tzimisce] <b><i>is</i></b> Clan Tzimisce. They are all just extensions of itself, more so than any other clan founder to its clan. Through its blood it became legion, rather than one being. It cares for its progeny like you care for individual skin cells. They do their thing, and if you lose a few here and there, who cares.<br /> <br /> The only other clan that comes close to Tzimisce are the Malkavians with the Malkavian Madness Network, but Malkav exerts for less control on his progeny, where [Tzimisce] can and will manifest through any of them if it feels like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not necessarily true to begin with. As every other story about Antediluvian transcendence it\u2019s just a suggestion/legend instead of factual truth within the setting.<br /> <br /> But even setting this aside, it\u2019s out of place in this discussion. The clan Tzimisce isn\u2019t particularly dangerous if it is secretly a single person (which is even kinda boring). That\u2019s the point <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"970\" data-vbnamecard=\"970\">Gurkhal</a> tried to make, this doesn\u2019t make the clan more or less dangerous as a clan, regardless of being true or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T23:05:43-07:00","id":1543736,"title":"","content":"Both Malkav and Tziscme might have moved past having a single body, but it doesn't mean either clan lost all free will and I believe that both antiduilveans only have so much control over there progeny and to my headcannon that they have the best luck influencing members of the 4th-6th generations and the further down the line you go the less influence.<br /> <br /> For instance my 11th generation Malkavian ties to the network is quite weak and might hear the odd stray thought from the rest of the clan, but Malkav influence would be minor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T18:53:09-07:00","id":1543809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543731#post1543731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not necessarily true to begin with. As every other story about Antediluvian transcendence it\u2019s just a suggestion/legend instead of factual truth within the setting.<br /> <br /> But even setting this aside, it\u2019s out of place in this discussion. The clan Tzimisce isn\u2019t particularly dangerous if it is secretly a single person (which is even kinda boring). That\u2019s the point <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"970\" data-vbnamecard=\"970\">Gurkhal</a> tried to make, this doesn\u2019t make the clan more or less dangerous as a clan, regardless of being true or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, who are you to decide what is appropriate for a discussion? This is the second time you've come to derail a thread with &quot;Nah bro, its not canon/fact.&quot;<br /> <br /> My person, anything written in the books, as long as its got that nice bit about being published by <b>White Wolf</b> (or a license holder like OPP) directly, is canon to the setting, and is a thing that is a fact to the setting. The argument that information found in the fiction is some how any less &quot;factual&quot; to the setting is absurd. If that's the case, nearly everything about <i>Hunter</i> is &quot;nonfactual&quot; since 95% of <i>Hunter</i> is written through the fiction. The fiction is what informs the setting and regardless of how unreliable <b>you</b> think the narrators are, does not diminish its importance. That's your head canon, and right as ST to use or not use the information is presented. The information is presented, and then sometimes even contradicted later with retcons and edition changes. In that case the newest information is the most canon, unless, again you want to disregard it.<br /> <br /> &quot;But but its all legends and hearsay and mythology&quot; you decry. This is World of Darkness friend. The WHOLE point of the setting is that legends and apocrypha are true. In the VtM setting, there was a literal God, and it cursed a literal Caine, and vampires literally exist. The whole setting is a fiction, set up to tell stories. Until the retcons of OPP with the release and continuation of the VtM setting, Caine literally hung out with Beckett for awhile and went on a fun world spanning adventure, while Lasombra himself ravaged a country as a shadow beast released from the Abyss, and Haquim tested his own childre as sand tornado of death. (This was the Gehenna Novel by the way.)<br /> <br /> Secondly, the Eldest was shown to use this power of manifesting through his blood multiple times, through legend, and in the direct fiction. It was a WHOLE plot point in the Tzimisce novels (Dark Ages, the character in particular was Ilias cel Frumos), and I believe it also shows up in Transylvania Chronicles. As you would say, this is factual truth within the setting. In the <b>now</b> non-canon Gehenna book scenario, he again nearly destroys the world single handedly by becoming one with everything and everyone.<br /> <br /> The original discussion, as you have seem to have glanced over was:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carsusbloodking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous#post1539068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it says in the title which of the clans do you think is the most dangerous in a variety of contexts including against kine, other kindred, other splats, politically? Basically, any way you can think of violence or domination of some kind, and why? I know it is open but that's the point for the purposes of conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what Clan is the most dangerous in 5th edition, 20th, Revised, or Second edition specifically. Not which Clan is the most dangerous according to some strict definition of canon. This is a thread in the VtM forums, and encompasses all information that has been officially produced for VtM.<br /> <br /> I was saddened because the conversation devolved into an argument strictly about powers like some VS thread about super heroes (well Spider-man can beat Ironman because he has X power and book Y shows the upper limit of this etc), because there are more facets to the Clans, and setting than just powers. My original choice, with the original discussion presented with the OP was the Caitiff (though technically not a clan and more of a faction but neither are bloodlines technically not clans,) because of the effect they have against the entirety of the Cainite species. They're not powerful individually, but politically they cause such a ripple effect that they are one of the Prophecies of Gehenna.<br /> <br /> Yet, if the discussion was going to turn to just disciplines, then my choice again, is the Tzimisce, for the reasons I said before. Like all clans, the Tzimisce are pawns of their nigh-god-like founder. Unlike all clans, they are direct extensions of its will and power through his mastery of the discipline Vicissitude, as well as <b>anyone</b> whom has <b>ever</b> tasted their vitae. This includes all of the Sabbat, the Tremere (who made themselves through Tzimisce vitae,) the Gargoyles, the Revanant families, and most likely all of the Ravnos of Hazimel's line, not to mention all the individuals these groups may have interacted with. This makes the Tzimisce as I said before a part of a larger organism, that is their founder, and are akin to individual autonomous cells, until it decides to exert control over them. [Tzimisce] is no longer one person, but multitudes, a gestalt of the best and worst of life and unlife. If you don't think a clan that is a physical extension of a nigh-god-like eldritch being is dangerous then I don't have much else to say to you on the subject.<br /> <br /> Its the same concept (or trope if you will) of the Grey Goo, Skynet, and many other legions that have been shown through the ages of fiction and its terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T19:17:16-07:00","id":1543811,"title":"","content":"This is just a suggestion of mine, but I think it's best to disregard the third generation in this conversation, I mean, they can decimate an entire clan if they want so it kind of loses its purpose and becomes a question about which antediluvian is stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T20:06:27-07:00","id":1543817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543809#post1543809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Firstly, who are you to decide what is appropriate for a discussion? This is the second time you've come to derail a thread with &quot;Nah bro, its not canon/fact.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t said it was inappropriate, I said it was out of place. Not the same thing.<br /> <br /> Gehenna, the book, along with some other supplements, says directly that the destiny of the Antediluvians is non-canon. In the same way, the setting is wholly based on the levels of unreliability of its narrators by design. You can take everything at face value if you want, but as many times as needed I\u2019ll say it isn\u2019t canon.<br /> <br /> But what I tried to say wasn\u2019t that you can\u2019t hold your opinion or anything. It was that using the Antediluvian as reason for the clan being dangerous is awkward at best. It\u2019s completely ignoring the clan whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:42:38-07:00","id":1543874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1542933#post1542933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here is where frequencies and averages play their parts.<br /> <br /> A PC Nos can be easily built to pull this off reliably. An average Nos, while expected to have the general skillset to do so, can\u2019t be expected to be so good, unless we\u2019re talking at least Ancillae. Here is where Merits being a rare thing in the setting is relevant, as you can\u2019t expect most Nos in the city to be able to fool security cameras, and so on.<br /> <br /> Shared tactics add the problem that this means regular use. If a tactic is possible, but only the most skilled in the clan would use it, then there\u2019s no reason to expect it to be shared.<br /> <br /> We know by how their clan culture is described what the shared tactics of the Nos are. They do use their Obfuscate to collect information, and they share this information among themselves. The Nosferatu are known as the main information brokers in the setting, and they certainly didn\u2019t got there by respecting people\u2019s privacy.<br /> <br /> That said, though, fabricated scenarios are far more delicate and potentially harmful to their business if someone is caught doing it. You need a lot of skill and risk taking to pull it off, the results aren\u2019t reliable, and being caught can not only result in harsh punishment, but would jeopardize the entire clan\u2019s thing in the city.<br /> <br /> It is, as I said earlier, a valid option for a PC, or even for an NPC with the right combination of skill, ambition and circumstance. But as a \u201creason to fear the clan\u201d, I highly doubt it would figure among their shared tactics, quite the opposite: they would discourage such behavior, so to not create needless problem<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the delay, had two weeks of mandatory overtime.<br /> <br /> I would venture Nos select childer for those required skills more often than average so it may be less a reach. Compare to other clans like Brujah(who will take an idealist or a warlord), the Toreador(who will take those cunning or simply pretty with little regard for skill), etc. Nos, Venture, Tremere, is the more structured clans I would say on average pick more uniform childer. <br /> <br /> And plus Neonate status can last, what, 100 years? That's a long time not to develop a skill set the clan heavily favors. <br /> <br /> And Ancillary and especially Elders would be on average, experienced, in that tactic, I would think.<br /> <br /> RE shared tactics, I disagree. A school of boxers all share the same skill sets, generally, but won't share the same advanced skills? I was a very average amateur kickboxer back in the day and actually impressed an IBF Title holder boxer by using an advanced technique. He kept asking about my coach and where he trained. He stated many pros didn't even know that tech. I thought it was common knowledge. Everyone in our class was shown it and could use it. <br /> <br /> Same with pack animals that share skills through play and mimicry. The advantageous skills will get passed along. <br /> <br /> As far as Nos credibility and privacy, a real world analog would be banks. <br /> <br /> They rip off most people all the time and people still use them. Fees disguised as important services are just cash grabs. On a larger scale, what, back in 2011(?) HSBC got caught running billions of dollars of drug money from drug lords to NYC to the Vatican. They were issues a small fee as punishment. <br /> <br /> Vamps don't really have many alternatives to the Nosferatu and remember - their founder was a legendary HUNTER(and Trapper by inference). Why WOULDNT an Info/Intelligence Cartel not abuse their holdings? Everyone else does, right?<br /> <br /> Fund managers fail all the time, yet the Fund stays strong and goes on. They lose sums of money we can only dream of because if that manager doesnt take that risk, they lose their jobs to those who do and succeed. Beat the Market or get fired.<br /> <br /> It literally called 'the Risk Curve'.<br /> <br /> Tell me vamps aren't that competitive? That Venture won't push an edge, or Tremere won't risk it all for more magical power, or a Tzimisce wont risk ruining themselves to idealize their flesh, etc <br /> <br /> IMO, you fear the Nosferatu because they are the masters of the unseen(everyone assumes Auspex is an automatic counter), their founder was a Hunter, and if you look at their survival strategy, it heavily implies Intelligence Operation. <br /> <br /> They have the dirt on YOU, they can make up dirt on you and make it believable to everyone else, they can supply info to either/both of two feuding sides and leverage it to pick a winner should they care. They have easier access to blood. Natural defense just by virtue of having the skills to not be dependent upon a city. They have clan unity which only few clans have. They are well enough received in all Sects. <br /> <br /> People go to the Nos for info when they are in NEED. That's weakness. And what do vampires do with weakness? Like taking a loan from the mob, right? Or one of the major banks. One seems exotic and dangerous, the other mundane and boring. Both, leave you with no alternative.<br /> <br /> I swear, no one fears the Nosferatu until they see someone play a Nos Arsonist. Neonates with those skills can be brutally threatening should they let their reputation slip. Otherwise, it looks like the city has an Anarch or Sabbat problem...<br /> <br /> And it's not like such a character would to that every night. It's a rare spice that adds magic to a dish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:46:38-07:00","id":1543876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543092#post1543092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If its about disciplines, then Tzimisce wins. That's it. Game over. The Eldest has infected a full 2/3 the Kindred population. He owns the entirety of the Sabbat, the Tremere, and anyone who has ever shared vitae with either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to think that. Not anymore.<br /> <br /> Because several other clans can claim the same. <br /> <br /> Venture IS living in the minds of his childer and possibly anyone they have ever used Dominate/Presence on. The discipline spread heavily insinuates it <br /> <br /> Malkav, similar. <br /> <br /> Gangrel can turn into the Sun(or some such )<br /> <br /> Lasombra can become and shadow, even the ones inside your body.<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> It all gets abstract in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:48:41-07:00","id":1543878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543736#post1543736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both Malkav and Tziscme might have moved past having a single body, but it doesn't mean either clan lost all free will and I believe that both antiduilveans only have so much control over there progeny and to my headcannon that they have the best luck influencing members of the 4th-6th generations and the further down the line you go the less influence.<br /> <br /> For instance my 11th generation Malkavian ties to the network is quite weak and might hear the odd stray thought from the rest of the clan, but Malkav influence would be minor.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really about how a given ST wants to use and write-inbthe Antes. <br /> <br /> IMO, they are not characters but Lore and plot-points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T15:43:36-07:00","id":1543918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543876#post1543876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I used to think that. Not anymore.<br /> <br /> Because several other clans can claim the same.<br /> <br /> Venture IS living in the minds of his childer and possibly anyone they have ever used Dominate/Presence on. The discipline spread heavily insinuates it<br /> <br /> Malkav, similar.<br /> <br /> Gangrel can turn into the Sun(or some such )<br /> <br /> Lasombra can become and shadow, even the ones inside your body.<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> It all gets abstract in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll concede this is a great point, but also argue that unlike the other Antes; [Tzimisce] is the only one with the potential to become the world wide food supply itself. Ventru, Malkav, Set and most likely Toreador ascend into the &quot;psychic vampire hivemind&quot; and control masses, but eventually [Tzimisce] subsumes their flesh anyway. [Lasombra] controls abyssal shadow creatures and shadows, but will eventually starve. Ennoia and [Tzimisce] would be on pretty equal terms in the planet melting world destroying bit, as they can both meld with the planet in different ways, and yeah Body of the Sun would pose a big problem except... eventually Ennoia would run out of sustenance before [Tzimisce] runs out of Reform Body.<br /> <br /> Augustus is MIA and might be dead. Ravnos is mostly dead. Brujah/Troile is good as dead. This leaves... Nosferatu/Absmilliard, who is just a huge coward imo.<br /> <br /> I get what you mean though, which is why I still think the Caitiff are the most dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T16:02:38-07:00","id":1543920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543918#post1543918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll concede this is a great point, but also argue that unlike the other Antes; [Tzimisce] is the only one with the potential to become the world wide food supply itself. Ventru, Malkav, Set and most likely Toreador ascend into the &quot;psychic vampire hivemind&quot; and control masses, but eventually [Tzimisce] subsumes their flesh anyway. [Lasombra] controls abyssal shadow creatures and shadows, but will eventually starve. Ennoia and [Tzimisce] would be on pretty equal terms in the planet melting world destroying bit, as they can both meld with the planet in different ways, and yeah Body of the Sun would pose a big problem except... eventually Ennoia would run out of sustenance before [Tzimisce] runs out of Reform Body.<br /> <br /> Augustus is MIA and might be dead. Ravnos is mostly dead. Brujah/Troile is good as dead. This leaves... Nosferatu/Absmilliard, who is just a huge coward imo.<br /> <br /> I get what you mean though, which is why I still think the Caitiff are the most dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll do you one better.<br /> <br /> Ravinos is the most powerful. Chimerstry10 lets it create reality.<br /> <br /> It wanted to save Humanity from Gehenna so I changed reality into a TTRPG. One the Tzimisce is stuck inside.<br /> <br /> But back to Tzimisce, is dilution factored in? Can one Ante become all things? What if it's not Tzimisce but Kupala? Seems too powerful for a 3rd Gen vampire. <br /> <br /> Absimilliard a coward? How would anyone know? Obfuscate10 likely makes him unknown. Gone from history and has no name. Seems like all the other Antes and Ancients would envy that ability. He could be killing other Antes and no one would be the wiser. <br /> <br /> Ultimately it's all conjecture and story crafting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T16:28:21-07:00","id":1543923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543920#post1543920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll do you one better.<br /> <br /> Ravinos is the most powerful. Chimerstry10 lets it create reality.<br /> <br /> It wanted to save Humanity from Gehenna so I changed reality into a TTRPG. One the Tzimisce is stuck inside.<br /> <br /> But back to Tzimisce, is dilution factored in? Can one Ante become all things? What if it's not Tzimisce but Kupala? Seems too powerful for a 3rd Gen vampire.<br /> <br /> Absimilliard a coward? How would anyone know? Obfuscate10 likely makes him unknown. Gone from history and has no name. Seems like all the other Antes and Ancients would envy that ability. He could be killing other Antes and no one would be the wiser.<br /> <br /> Ultimately it's all conjecture and story crafting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha. I like that.<br /> <br /> Absimilliard's existence being known about and the fact that his lineage fear him and his Nicktuku as boogeymen wanting to wipe them out, means he massively failed or botched to use Obfuscate to erase himself from the world as a known factor, otherwise when you ask the Nosferatu who created them they would go &quot;i dunno, we don't have a founder, we just exist.&quot; No Nosferatu would have enough Auspex to pierce his godlike Obfuscate, and the Clan is OBSESSED with him and his genocide of them. One of the descriptions of botching Memories Fading Glimpse was to become a beacon instead of removing yourself.<br /> <br /> He's a coward because he turned coat after the slaying of the 2nd generation immediately, even though he was so vindictive about Zilla scarring him, and decided to try to offer his progeny in contrition. The other 3rd gens took their curses like Chads, and just dealt with the consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T07:07:44-07:00","id":1544097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1543923#post1543923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ha. I like that.<br /> <br /> Absimilliard's existence being known about and the fact that his lineage fear him and his Nicktuku as boogeymen wanting to wipe them out, means he massively failed or botched to use Obfuscate to erase himself from the world as a known factor, otherwise when you ask the Nosferatu who created them they would go &quot;i dunno, we don't have a founder, we just exist.&quot; No Nosferatu would have enough Auspex to pierce his godlike Obfuscate, and the Clan is OBSESSED with him and his genocide of them. One of the descriptions of botching Memories Fading Glimpse was to become a beacon instead of removing yourself.<br /> <br /> He's a coward because he turned coat after the slaying of the 2nd generation immediately, even though he was so vindictive about Zilla scarring him, and decided to try to offer his progeny in contrition. The other 3rd gens took their curses like Chads, and just dealt with the consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But is it really fact, in a setting with unreliable narrators? And Obfuscate can let you appear as others... is that image of Absimilliard even true?<br /> <br /> What if Zillah 'the Beautiful' was really only so beautiful due to Obfuscate11? Just an aside.<br /> <br /> So heres some headcannon for you: i tend to see the Clans and their cultures/discipline spreads as survival strategies. Fuzzies up the Lore to loosen up expectations and remove predictability and Player expectation. <br /> <br /> Nosferatu was a legendary Hunter back in his breathing day as the story goes. All i need to know. Full Stop. He supposedly rebelled against his Elders and got his ass kicked. Maybe important. Maybe not.<br /> <br /> What i see is a Clan of hunters(arent they all??) that uses camouflage and ambush. Trapping as well, which is where the 'info broker' comes to play. Hunters need to know the habits and tendencies of their prey This is the lower level game the neonates and ancilla play. Hunters will eventually realize that the apex predator in an environment is susceptible to sudden collapse by changes in environment, they over-specialize, etc. What would the Elders and Ancients hunt???<br /> <br /> So to keep his kids sharp, Nosferatu used Animalism10(part of his Beast, to animate) + Obfuscate10(appear in other peoples minds) + Potence10(give a thought force) to make a 'what hunts the hunter?' scenario. Lazy Nos get hunted and motivated to stay sharp. Any other clan ever seen a Niktuku? Im not super versed in the Lore but im not thinking of a case where non-Nosferatu witnessed a Niktuku.<br /> <br /> I can do the same to Ventrue: The Rulers. Dominate(Letter of the(rather His) Law) + Presence(Spirit of the Law) + Fortitude(continues over time). Ventrue died(or faked it - not uncommon among Ventrue) and lives in the minds and blood of his descendants. Possibly in the minds of others as well? So Governments, Corporations, and Familial Cults are their hunting grounds.<br /> <br /> Malkav: the Disruptors. Auspex(to see the mind) + Dominate(to change the mind) + Obfuscate(by hiding things). they hunt by disrupting the status quo in an environment. Many seers and shamans are tricksters and shysters that will work the crowd. What if the Malkav's madness was the founder just hiding certain functions of their mind as a test and as a defense mechanism?<br /> <br /> So did 'Absimilliard' actually fail?<br /> <br /> And as a coward? Compared to what? Its like, wouldnt they all be failures if their Humanity dropped low enough?<br /> <br /> Others took their Curse like Chads??<br /> <br /> Lasombra likely fell to a Cthulhu shadow entity, he played with fire...er shadow and got burned. Tzimisce...depending on story and interpretation, got Hentai'd by some demon or space virus which was not even his original curse?. Malkav despite all the power couldnt keep his shit together. Toreador is a voyeur creep. Eww. Ventrue got punked by the Brujah/one of his kids/etc and became picky eaters. Set got bit doing kinky things with snakes and cant tolerate fire as well as other vamps...who cant tolerate fire? Tremere was 'Topped from the Bottom' so to speak(ill never forget when my friend described it as that - table burst out laughing). Brujah(i omit the true brujah out of how corny it is) couldnt run a city...and became...angry Communists??? Saulot...well that shit is complicated and so seeped in edgelordism you have to know about Gnostic Dualism/Sabbatean Frankism/Sadhus/etc to make any sense of it, other than the writers were looking for even a bigger bag, bigger than kaiju bad, a big bad soooooooooooooooooooo bad hes actually doing good!!!. Giovanni?- Tremere part 2 family boogaloo edition. Ravnos...no one even cares and got retconned out of being a trickster figure. Assamite got retconned from bloodthirsty assassin to...demon hunter? <br /> <br /> Im not sure any Ante should be looked upon favorably. They are walking mythic curses that kinda imply to never strive to become that powerful. Original 7 also imply the 7 Deadly Sins personified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T16:42:52-07:00","id":1544149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InspectorG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1544097#post1544097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But is it really fact, in a setting with unreliable narrators? And Obfuscate can let you appear as others... is that image of Absimilliard even true?<br /> <br /> What if Zillah 'the Beautiful' was really only so beautiful due to Obfuscate11? Just an aside.<br /> <br /> So heres some headcannon for you: i tend to see the Clans and their cultures/discipline spreads as survival strategies. Fuzzies up the Lore to loosen up expectations and remove predictability and Player expectation.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu was a legendary Hunter back in his breathing day as the story goes. All i need to know. Full Stop. He supposedly rebelled against his Elders and got his ass kicked. Maybe important. Maybe not.<br /> <br /> What i see is a Clan of hunters(arent they all??) that uses camouflage and ambush. Trapping as well, which is where the 'info broker' comes to play. Hunters need to know the habits and tendencies of their prey This is the lower level game the neonates and ancilla play. Hunters will eventually realize that the apex predator in an environment is susceptible to sudden collapse by changes in environment, they over-specialize, etc. What would the Elders and Ancients hunt???<br /> <br /> So to keep his kids sharp, Nosferatu used Animalism10(part of his Beast, to animate) + Obfuscate10(appear in other peoples minds) + Potence10(give a thought force) to make a 'what hunts the hunter?' scenario. Lazy Nos get hunted and motivated to stay sharp. Any other clan ever seen a Niktuku? Im not super versed in the Lore but im not thinking of a case where non-Nosferatu witnessed a Niktuku.<br /> <br /> I can do the same to Ventrue: The Rulers. Dominate(Letter of the(rather His) Law) + Presence(Spirit of the Law) + Fortitude(continues over time). Ventrue died(or faked it - not uncommon among Ventrue) and lives in the minds and blood of his descendants. Possibly in the minds of others as well? So Governments, Corporations, and Familial Cults are their hunting grounds.<br /> <br /> Malkav: the Disruptors. Auspex(to see the mind) + Dominate(to change the mind) + Obfuscate(by hiding things). they hunt by disrupting the status quo in an environment. Many seers and shamans are tricksters and shysters that will work the crowd. What if the Malkav's madness was the founder just hiding certain functions of their mind as a test and as a defense mechanism?<br /> <br /> So did 'Absimilliard' actually fail?<br /> <br /> And as a coward? Compared to what? Its like, wouldnt they all be failures if their Humanity dropped low enough?<br /> <br /> Others took their Curse like Chads??<br /> <br /> Lasombra likely fell to a Cthulhu shadow entity, he played with fire...er shadow and got burned. Tzimisce...depending on story and interpretation, got Hentai'd by some demon or space virus which was not even his original curse?. Malkav despite all the power couldnt keep his shit together. Toreador is a voyeur creep. Eww. Ventrue got punked by the Brujah/one of his kids/etc and became picky eaters. Set got bit doing kinky things with snakes and cant tolerate fire as well as other vamps...who cant tolerate fire? Tremere was 'Topped from the Bottom' so to speak(ill never forget when my friend described it as that - table burst out laughing). Brujah(i omit the true brujah out of how corny it is) couldnt run a city...and became...angry Communists??? Saulot...well that shit is complicated and so seeped in edgelordism you have to know about Gnostic Dualism/Sabbatean Frankism/Sadhus/etc to make any sense of it, other than the writers were looking for even a bigger bag, bigger than kaiju bad, a big bad soooooooooooooooooooo bad hes actually doing good!!!. Giovanni?- Tremere part 2 family boogaloo edition. Ravnos...no one even cares and got retconned out of being a trickster figure. Assamite got retconned from bloodthirsty assassin to...demon hunter?<br /> <br /> Im not sure any Ante should be looked upon favorably. They are walking mythic curses that kinda imply to never strive to become that powerful. Original 7 also imply the 7 Deadly Sins personified.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Niktuku, the only one that shows up in any book AFAIK, was in Nights of Prophecy story where one kills Baba Yaga, and the Niktuku suffers from Ur-Shulgi syndrome. Comes in, does a thing, and sits around being invulnerable till it gets bored and slinks away. This story had Kindred, Mages, and Garou abound, oh my. Its also implied the Niktuku Dominate/Animalism/Presence controls a pack of Garou.<br /> <br /> In V20 Dark Ages, they made Niktuku a bloodline, which basically makes them like CoD Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> On Zillah. She was called Zillah the Beautiful before she was embraced, because that was the reason she was embraced. Caine was in love with her, and forced a blood bond on her to make her his. (Via Book of Nod) She broke Nosferatu as a mortal, and scarred him. His vanity caused him to attack her again after the embrace with his childer. He again for a third time attacks her with the rest of the Ante's and may have/may not have finaly killed her.<br /> <br /> The common theme is that the Ante's curses came from Caine himself, this is echoed in the Book of Nod, Erinyes Fragments, and other sources. When Caine showed up and laid down the law, every Ante other than Nosferatu accepted their curse for their sins, but Nosferatu was the only one to beg forgiveness, and attempt to immediately genocide his progeny in contrition. Just as Caine had too much pride, and wouldn't yield, his grand-childer other than Nosferatu did the same.<br /> <br /> Yes, they shouldn't be looked on favorably, but we are allowed to have favorite villains and characters. Absmilliard/Nosferatu is one of my least favorite.<br /> <br /> Claiming unreliable narrator is frankly lazy. (This isn't directed at you specifically, I've seen the unreliable narrator claim a bunch lately..) Yes much of the back story is myth and legend, but myths and legends always hide truth within them. If you discount everything as unreliable narrator, then you might as well throw away the WHOLE history of the kindred (and hell every other White Wolf line but then why are we here playing this game in the first place?), and make up your own, since you can't be sure of ANYTHING, even the things people generally take as iron clad fact. There is a point where you have to stop and look at the information actually published and say, &quot;Well they imply things this way, so unless I want to head canon it some other way, this is how they meant it to be.&quot; Yes things change between editions. Yes things get retconned. Yes many people worked on different books and had different visions, scopes, and ideas. White Wolf lines are fiction, wrapped up with mechanical rules to allow you to play a game and tell a story, and while you can change that story and make that story how ever you wish, the authors have laid a bedrock of information for the players and readers to play in.<br /> <br /> Is that image of Absmilliard true? There's no telling, but there is more evidence that it is, rather than not, and Occam's Razor says that some times a spade is just a spade. Besides though, Transylvania chronicles does confirm a few things about him, as did the now non-canon (but hey [I say this jokingly...] its only non-canon if you accept V20 or 5th exist...) Gehenna books.<br /> <br /> I like your head canon. That's a fun &quot;modern&quot; Darwinistic approach. Dr. Neturch would be proud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T14:52:57-07:00","id":1544360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539068-which-of-the-clans-is-the-most-dangerous?p=1544149#post1544149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your head canon. That's a fun &quot;modern&quot; Darwinistic approach. Dr. Neturch would be proud.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few tables played Lore-agnostic and Clanless(everyone was essentially Caitiff) and many of us just came to the conclusion the Lore was a buffet to choose from. One of the best interpretations of the Brujah was one ST thought that they werent impassioned by ideals, they were really impassioned by inflicting said ideal upon others. Warlords essentially. Then the philosopher/anarchist dichotomy doesnt really matter, it boils down to which Brujah can rule the roost.<br /> <br /> RE unreliable narrator, it lent to the big bads because the less you define them, the more power they keep. Plus the whole, gehenna plot painted the franchise into a corner, which resulted in Requiem being a lot less defined, right?<br /> <br /> Also, the WoD has supernatural entities with powers that can muddy narrative easily. My previous example of Nos using Obfuscate to hide history. But also think of Presence and Dominate that can be used to shape, even force, an interpretation of an event onto others. And like in Requiem, Vamps dont have perfect memory anyways. Requiem just leaned upon that factor more to hide the past. So IMO, Unreliable Narrator fits this system well.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}